(7645565, 1242458, 163081, '<td valign="top">The 1200pxl compression lost much detail. It is not an easy shot. The hike is a 30minutes steep climb to reach this lookout. <br/>This time I tried to get the starlight effect of the light on the top of the Taipei101. Very happy with the result.<br/></td>', 'The 1200pxl compression lost much detail. It is not an easy shot. The hike is a 30minutes steep climb to reach this lookout. This time I tried to get the starlight effect of the light on the top of the Taipei101. Very happy with the result.', '2019-11-06 12:21:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7645584, 1242607, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> That''s right. Nice. But, blue?<br/> <br/>hi<br/>I can understand the reaction to the blue.  this was taken 15 miles away - 7 image vert pano - for some reason that filter helped the skyline itself pop.  This was done an hour prior to golden hour sadly (no other choice). I should have used a gradient to bring the green trees up a notch to contrast better.<br/>Jim<br/> <br/>Perhaps because when I took a similar image (with my phone, from behind the dirty glass), everything was yellowish I reacted to the blue tonality.<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1242861" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/120000-124999/124815/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1242861.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/120000-124999/124815/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1242861.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/120000-124999/124815/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1242861.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: That''s right. Nice. But, blue? hiI can understand the reaction to the blue.  this was taken 15 miles away - 7 image vert pano - for some reason that filter helped the skyline itself pop.  This was done an hour prior to golden hour sadly (no other choice). I should have used a gradient to bring the green trees up a notch to contrast better.Jim Perhaps because when I took a similar image (with my phone, from behind the dirty glass), everything was yellowish I reacted to the blue tonality. ', '2019-11-06 15:43:23.000000', NULL, 0),
